<title>USA: U.S. Feb durable goods orders rose 1.5 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Feb durable goods orders rose 1.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	Feb     Jan--Rev from     Dec</p>
<p>  New Orders		  1.5     4.1     4.0	-1.7</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.  -3.6     1.6     2.5	-0.6</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.     3.1     4.9     2.5	-2.1</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	 1.5     5.4     5.2	-1.4</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders	0.1   -21.6   -20.2	-8.1</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders   3.7     4.5     5.3	Unch</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts    6.9     3.2     3.9	-2.2</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Feb	Jan---Rev from    Dec</p>
<p> New Orders		178.32   175.77   175.67    168.89</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  40.83    42.35    42.69     41.67</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   137.49   133.42     N/A     127.22</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     172.00   169.45   169.24    160.83</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	6.32     6.32     6.43	8.06</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  47.55    45.85    46.21     43.87</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   40.52    37.91    38.16     36.74</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	Feb     Jan--Rev from     Dec</p>
<p> Total Shipments	    1.4     1.1     1.2	-0.8</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders    1.1     1.1     1.0	Unch</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Feb	Jan---Rev from    Dec</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 172.97   170.56   170.76    168.72</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   499.48   494.13   493.82    488.91</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES   Feb     Jan--Rev from     Dec</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	   -0.5     5.1     5.2	 4.4</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery    2.2     0.9     1.6	 2.1</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery    7.4    17.9    16.6     -13.8</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  15.81    15.89   15.90     15.11</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  33.22    32.50   32.72     32.21</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  30.56    28.46   28.14     24.13</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected February durable goods orders to fall 0.4 percent. Excluding defense orders, they expected a 0.6 percent drop.</p>
<p>The department said the February durable goods orders were a record high $178.32 billion.</p>
<p>Durable goods orders excluding transportation and excluding defense also were at record high levels in February, Commerce said.</p>
<p>It said all components of transportation equipment orders fell in February except for railroad equipment.</p>
</text>
